function codegraphGitConfig(): Record<string, string> {
  const entries = [
    ...GIT_SAFE_CONFIG.filter((arg) => arg !== '-c'),
    'core.splitIndex=false',
    'diff.ignoreSubmodules=all',
    'status.submoduleSummary=false',
  ];
  const env: Record<string, string> = { GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: String(entries.length) };
  entries.forEach((entry, index) => {
    const equals = entry.indexOf('=');
    env[`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_${index}`] = entry.slice(0, equals);
    env[`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_${index}`] = entry.slice(equals + 1);
  });
  return env;
}

findings.body:
**Concern.** Before this PR the conductor's first cut was a single `git worktree add`. git cleans up a failed or interrupted add itself (`remove_junk` runs on exit and on signals), so the next start cut again from scratch. Now the add is `--no-checkout` and the files come from a separate `checkoutPinned` (`read-tree --reset -u`). The launch and the fix round wrap that call in an undo (`dropUncheckedWorktree`, `dropUncheckedRound`). The conductor's first cut does not:

```ts
const tip = runGit(repoPath, ['rev-parse', '--verify', `refs/heads/${target}^{commit}`]).trim();
runGit(repoPath, ['worktree', 'add', '--detach', '--no-checkout', checkoutDir, tip]);
return checkoutPinned(repoPath, checkoutDir, tip);
```

**Triggers.** Ctrl-C during the first `pup conductor start` on a large repo (the read-tree is the slow part), ENOSPC, or any read-tree error partway through. Each leaves some files written and no index committed, while `<checkout>/.git` and the admin dir exist.

**Why it never heals.** Every later start takes:

```ts
if (existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git'))) {
  const git = verifiedWorktreeGitEnv(repoPath, checkoutDir);
  runGit(checkoutDir, ['checkout', '--detach', `refs/heads/${target}`], { env: { ...git } });
```

The pointers still verify. With no index, `checkout` does an initial checkout and refuses to overwrite the partial files as untracked. `prepareGraph` catches that, so each start prints "Could not index …" and runs without a graph, indefinitely. Decision 101 lists the conductor among the `--no-checkout` users but records undos only for the launch and the fix round. Its ceilings mention a graph lost "until the checkout is deleted and re-cut" only for a misnamed admin dir, not for this case. (The git behaviour is from git's source; it wasn't reproduced under CI.)

**Fix options.**
- Have the refresh path treat a checkout with no `<admin dir>/index` as half-cut and re-run `checkoutPinned(repoPath, checkoutDir, <target tip>)`. This also covers SIGINT, which a try/catch can't.
- At minimum, wrap the first cut's `checkoutPinned` the way the launch does: remove the dir, `worktree prune`, rethrow.

